<mjml>
  <mj-head>
    <mj-attributes>
      <mj-all font-family="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" />
      <mj-text font-size="15px" color="#242220" line-height="1.6" />
    </mj-attributes>
  </mj-head>
  <mj-body background-color="#f7f5f2">
    <!-- Brand header -->
    <mj-section background-color="#1B6549" padding="28px 24px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text align="center" font-size="26px" font-weight="bold" color="#ffffff">
          V-Vet
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Main card -->
    <mj-section background-color="#ffffff" padding="36px 32px 8px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text font-size="22px" font-weight="bold" padding-bottom="12px">
          Thanks for applying, {{ full_name|e }}
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text>
          We've received your application for the <strong>{{ role_title|e }}</strong> role.
          The next step is a short coding task. We review your application and your task
          together, so please send the task even while we're still reading your application.
        </mj-text>

        <mj-divider border-color="#E7E4DF" border-width="1px" padding="20px 0" />

        <mj-text font-size="18px" font-weight="bold">
          The task: a symptom extraction service
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text>
          Farmers describe sick animals to V-Vet on WhatsApp, in their own words. Before we can
          decide how urgent a case is, we turn those words into structured findings from a fixed
          list of signs. You'll build a small version of that.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text>
          Build a small Python API (FastAPI preferred) with one endpoint,
          <code>POST /extract</code>, that takes <code>{"message": "..."}</code> and returns:
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text font-family="Menlo, Consolas, monospace" font-size="13px" container-background-color="#f7f5f2" padding="16px 20px">
          {<br />
          &nbsp;&nbsp;"findings": [<br />
          &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;{"sign_id": "...", "value": "yes | no | not_sure", "quote": "..."}<br />
          &nbsp;&nbsp;],<br />
          &nbsp;&nbsp;"escalate": true,<br />
          &nbsp;&nbsp;"reason": "..."<br />
          }
        </mj-text>

        <mj-text font-weight="bold" padding-top="16px">The signs (sign_id: what it means)</mj-text>
        <mj-text>
          <ul style="margin:0;padding-left:20px;">
            <li><code>reduced_appetite</code>: eating less, or has stopped eating or grazing</li>
            <li><code>weakness</code>: dull, weak, lying down more than usual</li>
            <li><code>swelling</code>: a lump below the ear, under the jaw, or in front of the shoulder (farmers may call it <em>mbandabvu</em>)</li>
            <li><code>rapid_breathing</code>: breathing fast while resting</li>
            <li><code>cloudy_eye</code>: the eye looks white, grey or milky</li>
            <li><code>froth_nose_mouth</code>: foam or froth from the nose or mouth</li>
            <li><code>red_urine</code>: urine that is red, brown, or the colour of strong tea</li>
            <li><code>unable_to_stand</code>: cannot get up or stay standing</li>
            <li><code>ticks</code>: ticks can be seen on the animal</li>
          </ul>
        </mj-text>

        <mj-text font-weight="bold" padding-top="16px">Requirements</mj-text>
        <mj-text>
          <ol style="margin:0;padding-left:20px;">
            <li>Use an LLM to extract the findings. Any provider is fine, including free tiers. Validate the model's output so that only the sign IDs above can come back.</li>
            <li>Only report signs the message actually mentions. Use <code>not_sure</code> when the farmer sounds unsure.</li>
            <li>Decide <code>escalate</code> in plain code, not with the LLM: escalate when <code>froth_nose_mouth</code>, <code>unable_to_stand</code> or <code>cloudy_eye</code> is <code>yes</code> or <code>not_sure</code>.</li>
            <li>Write tests that run without a network connection or API key (mock the LLM).</li>
            <li>Include a README covering how to run it, the decisions you made, how you would measure whether the extraction is accurate, and what you would do with more time.</li>
          </ol>
        </mj-text>

        <mj-text font-weight="bold" padding-top="16px">Sample messages to try</mj-text>
        <mj-text>
          <ol style="margin:0;padding-left:20px;">
            <li>"My cow has not been eating since yesterday and she is breathing very fast."</li>
            <li>"There's foam coming from her nose and she can't get up."</li>
            <li>"I think the eyes look a bit cloudy but I'm not sure. She has mbandabvu under the ear."</li>
            <li>"The calf is fine, just lots of ticks on the ears."</li>
            <li>"Mombe yangu haisi kudya, and her urine is dark like tea."</li>
          </ol>
        </mj-text>

        <mj-text font-weight="bold" padding-top="16px">Time and tools</mj-text>
        <mj-text>
          Aim for about 3 to 4 hours, and don't over-polish: we care more about how you think than
          about finishing everything. You're welcome to use AI coding assistants. Tell us in the
          README how you used them, because we'll go through your code together at the interview.
        </mj-text>

        <mj-divider border-color="#E7E4DF" border-width="1px" padding="20px 0" />

        <mj-text font-size="18px" font-weight="bold">How to submit</mj-text>
        <mj-text>
          <ol style="margin:0;padding-left:20px;">
            <li>Push your code to a public GitHub repository. Don't commit any API keys.</li>
            <li>Email the link to <a href="mailto:{{ careers_email }}" style="color:#1B6549;">{{ careers_email }}</a> with the subject <strong>Coding task: {{ full_name|e }}</strong>.</li>
            <li>Please send it within 7 days of receiving this email.</li>
          </ol>
        </mj-text>

        <mj-text font-size="18px" font-weight="bold" padding-top="16px">What happens next</mj-text>
        <mj-text>
          Once your task arrives, we review it together with your application. If it's a good
          fit, we'll invite you to an interview, where we go through your code with you, do some
          live coding (you can use AI tools) and talk about how you work. We'll let you know
          either way.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text padding-bottom="28px">
          Questions? Reply to this email. Good luck, and thank you for your interest in V-Vet.
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- Footer -->
    <mj-section background-color="#f7f5f2" padding="20px 24px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text align="center" font-size="12px" color="#5C5A56">
          &copy; V-Vet 2026. Livestock health intelligence.
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
  </mj-body>
</mjml>
